<title>UK: Britannia denies talk of life business sale.</title>
<headline>Britannia denies talk of life business sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britannia Building Society on Tuesday denied it was considering the sale of Britannia Life, its Glasgow-based life company.</p>
<p>The denial followed a report in The Scotsman newspaper that approaches had been made to mutuals and banks in Scotland about buying the business, which has four billion pounds in assets and employs 850 people.</p>
<p>&quot;The report is factually incorrect,&quot; said a Britannia spokewoman.</p>
<p>&quot;Britannia has no plans to withdraw from the life insurance business and is fully supportive of Britannia Life plans for the future,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7721</p>
